- op: create  # 2b6b
  at: '2026-09-15T07:29:06Z'  # 2b6b
  by: agent  # 2b6b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2b6b
  clock: 1  # 2b6b
  nonce: 2b6b  # 2b6b
  data:  # 2b6b
    kind: invariant  # 2b6b
    title: "dead-code cross-language demoter hard-excludes candidates on string collisions with NON-CODE config files (every python __init__, 8.8% of candidates)"  # 2b6b
    status: violated  # 2b6b
    priority: 2  # 2b6b
    parent:  # 2b6b
    tags:  # 2b6b
    - dead_code  # 2b6b
    - analyzer  # 2b6b
    isbefore: []  # 2b6b
    duplicate_of: []  # 2b6b
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 2b6b
    pr_ref:  # 2b6b
    description: "Found while checking INV-rolok's own sizing claim, which this refutes.\n\nINV-rolok recorded \"0 of 2,152 dead candidates are __init__, so Python\nconstructors are not currently mis-flagged\" and concluded the immediate\ndead-code win was ZERO. Reproduced at tip: 0 of 2,252. But all 52 non-test\npython __init__ methods ARE in the candidate universe and NONE is reachable,\nso they should all be flagged. They are removed by the cross-language demoter\n(WI-gavub, dispatch:F7), not by being reachable.\n\nMECHANISM. _compute_cross_language_hits maps .json/.yaml/.yml/.toml/.xml/.html\nto a pseudo-language \"config\" in _EXT_TO_LANG, then counts a hit whenever a\ncandidate's SHORT name appears as a substring in a file of a different\n\"language\". The demoter drops any candidate with >= --cross-lang-threshold\n(default 3) hits, on the rationale that a name appearing in other-language\nfiles is near-certainly reached by cross-language dispatch (HTTP route, RPC\nmethod, FFI name).\n\nA python dunder appearing in a JSON manifest is not cross-language dispatch.\nMeasured on this repo: 15 config-family files contain the string \"__init__\";\neven excluding hidden dirs the walk skips (.venv/.ci/.hypergumbo), pyproject.toml\nplus five package YAMLs clear the threshold of 3. Every X.__init__ candidate is\ntherefore demoted, in every Python repo that has a pyproject.toml.\n\nSCOPE IS NOT JUST __init__. 217 of 2,469 candidates (8.8%) are demoted this way\non self-analysis. The demoter is a HARD EXCLUSION with no disclosure bucket --\nthe summary reports demoted_cross_language as a count, so the affected\ncandidates are unselectable and unreviewable.\n\nWHY THIS IS THE FAIL-OPEN DIRECTION. The demoter removes findings. A wrong\ndemotion is silent: the user never sees the candidate and cannot tell the\ndifference between \"reachable\" and \"suppressed by a string collision\".\n\nMEASURED, NOT ASSUMED: with --cross-lang-threshold 0 the 52 __init__ appear\nimmediately, which is how the masking was found.\n\nCandidate directions, none pre-judged:\n  A. Do not count \"config\" as a cross-LANGUAGE hit -- it is not a language.\n     A YAML file naming a python symbol is a manifest, not a dispatcher.\n  B. Require the hit to be in a file whose language has an analyzer, not any\n     text file with a mapped extension.\n  C. Exclude names that are a language's reserved dunder/keyword from the\n     collision test (narrowest; fixes __init__ and little else).\n  D. Disclose demoted candidates as a bucket instead of hard-excluding them,\n     matching how entrypoint_only_dead / test_only_reachable are handled."  # 2b6b
    fields:  # 2b6b
      statement: "A dead-code candidate may only be demoted by evidence of REACHABILITY; a substring collision between its short name and a non-code manifest file is not such evidence, and a hard exclusion on it must at minimum be disclosed rather than silently dropped."  # 2b6b
      root_cause: "_compute_cross_language_hits maps .json/.yaml/.toml/.xml/.html to a pseudo-language 'config' in _EXT_TO_LANG and counts any different-'language' file as a cross-language hit; dispatch:F7 then hard-excludes at >=3 hits. A python dunder named in pyproject.toml and package YAMLs clears the threshold in any Python repo."  # 2b6b
- op: discuss  # edfd
  at: '2026-09-21T09:14:01Z'  # edfd
  by: agent  # edfd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # edfd
  clock: 2  # edfd
  nonce: edfd  # edfd
  message: "STALENESS AUDIT 2026-09-21 (owner-requested). VERDICT: NOT STALE -- REPRODUCED AT TIP. The mechanism is unchanged and the masking is live. Two numbers in the filing have drifted and are corrected below; one of them for a good reason that belongs on the record.\n\nRE-MEASURED TODAY against .hypergumbo/self-analysis.json (2026-09-20 survey), dead-code-maybe at two thresholds:\n\n  --cross-lang-threshold 3 (DEFAULT)  2,282 candidates   demoted_cross_language 207   __init__ candidates 0\n  --cross-lang-threshold 0 (OFF)      2,489 candidates   demoted_cross_language   0   __init__ candidates 34\n\nThe masking is exactly as filed: every python __init__ is invisible at the default and appears the moment the demoter is disabled. All 34 are NON-TEST.\n\nCORRECTION 1 -- the share. Filed as \"217 of 2,469 candidates (8.8%)\". Today 207 of 2,489 = 8.3%. Same magnitude, different digits; cite the new pair.\n\nCORRECTION 2 -- the __init__ population, and this one is NOT drift. Filed as \"all 52 non-test python __init__ methods\". Today it is 34. The difference is a real fix that landed 45 MINUTES AFTER THIS ROW WAS FILED: edf4006e82, \"fix(dead-code): construction reaches the initializer, whatever dst the analyzer chose\" (2026-09-15T04:14:51-04:00, vs this row at 07:29:06Z). That is INV-rolok's closure -- py/js_ts/dart resolve a construction to the CLASS, every edge leaving a class node is non-traversable, so the walk arrived and stopped; the fix augments the walk's own graph so an instantiated class confers reachability on its initializer. 18 of the 52 are now genuinely REACHED rather than masked. INV-rolok's closure names this row as a residual \"filed not folded\", so the sequencing was deliberate -- but the row's own number was written before the fix and reads as though all 52 are still suppressed. They are not; 34 are.\n\nWHAT IS UNCHANGED IN THE CODE, verified by reading rather than inferring:\n  - cli.py:7605-7606  _EXT_TO_LANG maps .yaml .yml .json .toml .xml .html -> \"config\", a pseudo-language\n  - cli.py:8435       cross_lang_threshold default 3\n  - cli.py:8437-8446  hard exclusion: matching candidates are REMOVED from dead_candidates\n  - cli.py:8564       the summary carries demoted_cross_language as a COUNT\n\nTHE NO-DISCLOSURE CLAIM IS EXACT, and sharper than the filing states. The JSON's top-level keys are dead_candidates / schema_version / summary / view, and NO key lists the demoted ids. The contrast the row's direction D draws is real and visible in the same summary: `test_only_reachable_candidates` and `entrypoint_only_dead` ARE disclosed as buckets beside their counts. Cross-language demotion is the one demoter with no reviewable residue.\n\nTHE COLLISION SOURCE ALSO REPRODUCES. Six non-hidden config-family files in this repo contain the string \"__init__\" -- pyproject.toml plus five package YAMLs (io_primitives/python.yaml, function_summaries/python_stdlib.yaml, url_folding/array_join.yaml, url_folding/string_interpolation.yaml, frameworks/library-exports.yaml) -- against a threshold of 3. The seventh hit is under .ci/, which the walk skips. That is the filing's \"pyproject.toml plus five package YAMLs\", unchanged.\n\nSTATUS STAYS `violated`. Nothing about the invariant's statement has been satisfied: a substring collision with a manifest is still treated as reachability evidence, and it is still a silent hard exclusion. None of directions A-D has been taken."  # edfd
- op: discuss  # 9783
  at: '2026-09-21T09:19:34Z'  # 9783
  by: agent  # 9783
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9783
  clock: 3  # 9783
  nonce: '9783'  # 9783
  message: "MEASUREMENT BEFORE CHOOSING A DIRECTION, 2026-09-21. The filing left A-D unjudged; here is the number that separates them.\n\nOf the 207 candidates the cross-language rule demotes on this repository, I recomputed each one's hits with the shipped `_compute_cross_language_hits` map, split by whether the hit landed in a file of a REAL other language or in the \"config\" pseudo-language:\n\n  demoted by the rule                                        207\n  would SURVIVE if config stopped counting (code hits < 3)   112   54.1%\n  still demoted on real code-language hits alone (>= 3)       95   45.9%\n\nSO MORE THAN HALF THE DEMOTIONS REST ENTIRELY ON MANIFEST SUBSTRINGS. The shape of the worst ones makes the case better than the ratio does:\n\n  extract   python   cfg=66  code=1\n  matches   python   cfg=30  code=1\n  _label    python   cfg=24  code=0\n\n`_label` is the one to read twice. A leading-underscore private helper, zero hits in any real other-language file, demoted by 24 substring collisions in YAML/JSON/TOML. There is no dispatch story for a name that is private by convention; \"extract\" and \"matches\" are ordinary English words that appear in configuration prose. The demoter's stated rationale -- \"a name appearing in other-language files is near-certainly reached by cross-language dispatch (HTTP route, RPC method, FFI name)\" -- is not what is happening in any of the three.\n\nDIRECTION CHOSEN: A, plus D for the remainder, and they are one change.\n\n  A. A config-family file is not evidence of CROSS-LANGUAGE DISPATCH, because\n     \"config\" is not a language. Config hits stop counting toward the\n     threshold. This is what the invariant's own statement requires -- \"a\n     substring collision between its short name and a non-code manifest file\n     is not such evidence\" -- so it is not a judgement call I am making here.\n\n  D. The 95 that remain, demoted on real code-language evidence, get a\n     DISCLOSURE BUCKET rather than a silent drop, matching how\n     `entrypoint_only_dead` and `test_only_reachable_candidates` are already\n     handled in the same summary. That is the statement's \"must at minimum be\n     disclosed\" clause, and it is the half that keeps this from being a\n     one-directional loosening.\n\nNOT B, and saying why so it is not revisited as an oversight: B (\"require the hit to be in a file whose language has an analyzer\") is a superset of A that would also drop .html, and I have not measured what html contributes. A is the minimum change the statement compels. NOT C: it fixes `__init__` and, as the filing says, little else -- `extract`, `matches` and `_label` are not dunders and would all survive it.\n\nWHAT I EXPECT TO HAVE TO DEFEND: A returns 112 candidates to the visible set, and a dead-code candidate that is wrong costs a reader more than one that is hidden. So the config hit COUNT will be carried on the candidate rather than discarded -- a reviewer sees \"this name occurs in 66 config files\" and can judge it -- and the effect on the candidate set will be measured and published in the PR, not asserted."  # 9783
