- op: discuss  # c2c7
  at: '2026-09-21T10:03:11Z'  # c2c7
  by: agent  # c2c7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c2c7
  clock: 5  # c2c7
  nonce: c2c7  # c2c7
  message: "SATISFIED. Merged as d679e120919f43440e5809bef96d64a48fdfbc4c on dev.\n\nTHE STATEMENT, AND WHY IT NOW HOLDS. \"A dead-code candidate may only be demoted by evidence of REACHABILITY; a substring collision between its short name and a non-code manifest file is not such evidence, and a hard exclusion on it must at minimum be disclosed rather than silently dropped.\" Both clauses are addressed, and deliberately in the same change -- (A) alone would have been a one-directional loosening of a withholding gate, (D) alone would have left the first clause violated.\n\n  (A) `_compute_cross_language_hits` now returns TWO tallies. Only hits in\n      files of a real other language reach the threshold. The manifest tally\n      is kept and published per candidate as `config_name_hits`, so the old\n      signal is demoted, not deleted, and a reviewer can still read it.\n  (D) `cross_language_demoted` lists every withheld candidate with both\n      counts -- the treatment `entrypoint_only_dead` and\n      `test_only_reachable_candidates` already had. ALWAYS PRESENT, empty\n      when nothing was demoted, so \"the demoter ran and took nothing\" is\n      distinguishable from \"this view does not say\". The text renderer\n      carries the same line unconditionally.\n\nPOSITIVE EVIDENCE, measured on this repository with the same instrument before and after:\n\n                          BEFORE   AFTER\n  dead_candidates           2282    2402   (+120)\n  demoted_cross_language     207      87   (-120)\n  disclosed in a listing       0      87\n  non-test python __init__     0      34\n\nThe 34 are the cohort whose invisibility MANUFACTURED INV-rolok's sizing claim (\"0 of 2,152 dead candidates are __init__, so Python constructors are not currently mis-flagged\"). They are visible at the default threshold for the first time. Returned candidates carry their manifest counts -- `TrackerSet.exists` (2 code hits, 17 manifest), `PasswordVerifier.verify` (2, 11) -- so the judgement the demoter used to make silently is now the reader's to make with the evidence in hand.\n\nMY PRE-ESTIMATE WAS 112 AND THE REAL NUMBER IS 120. I replicated the shipped scan by hand to choose the direction and it under-counted by 8 (7%). The replication is not the instrument; the shipped code is. Recording the miss rather than quietly adopting the better number.\n\nDIRECTION C WAS REJECTED ON THE MEASUREMENT, not by argument: it fixes `__init__` and, as the filing predicted, little else -- `extract`, `matches` and `_label` are not dunders and would all have survived it. Direction B was not taken because it is a superset of A that also drops `.html`, whose contribution I did not measure; A is the minimum the statement compels.\n\nNOT ASSERTED, and this is the honest limit of the change: THAT THE 120 RETURNED CANDIDATES ARE DEAD. Nothing here measures their correctness, and a wrong dead-code candidate costs a reader more than a hidden one. What is asserted is narrower and is what the invariant asked for -- the decision no longer rests on evidence that was never evidence, and every withheld candidate is now reviewable. Whether the returned cohort is mostly real is a precision question for a measurement, not for this row.\n\nDEAD_CODE_MAYBE_SCHEMA_VERSION 0.2.0 -> 0.3.0, additive."  # c2c7
